Bubble Sort: 

    It's comparing the adjecent elements and swapping them if they are in the wrong order.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: Yes
    In-place: Yes

Selection Sort:

    It's finding the minimum element and swapping it with the first element.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: No
    In-place: Yes

Insertion Sort:

    It consists of 2 parts sorted array and unsorrted array, 
    first part is sorted and second part is unsorted.
    iterate through the unsorted part and insert the element at the right index in sorted part.
    Time Complexity: O(n^2)
    Space Complexity: O(1)
    Stable: Yes
    In-place: Yes

